    "Name": "Augustus A3 MBT",
    "Details": "The Augustus A-3 Tank was first developed during the Age of War. By 3075 the design had been obsolete for over seven centuries, however it was revisited by Brooks Incorporated when they were developing the new Moltke Main Battle Tank. Both tanks shared a very similar appearance with triple turret and sloping track guards.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Biome Restrictions: This unit can not deploy in Lunar or Martian biomes due to using an ICE.</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 3/5 hexes / 90/150 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Primitive Armor\n<b>Structure:</b> Primitive Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       240     40\n<b>Left</b>         155     40\n<b>Right</b>       155     40\n<b>Rear</b>        115     40\n<b>Turret</b>      190     40\n\n<b>Total</b>      855    200</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Improved Targeting - Long</color>\n\n<color=#ffcc00>Can Resupply/Repair</color>",
    "Icon": "MoltkeMBT"
  },
